<title>BELGIUM: SGB says sold Elf shares for 7 bln Bfr.</title>
<headline>SGB says sold Elf shares for 7 bln Bfr.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique said on Thursday the sale of most of its stake in French oil group Elf raised seven billion Belgian francs.</p>
<p>Confirming comments to Reuters earlier on Thursday, SGB said in a statement it had sold 2,880,000, or 80 percent, of its 3,600,000 Elf shares. Officials could not immediately comment on whether SGB booked a capital gain on the transaction.</p>
<p>SGB bought 1.6 percent of Elf at the time of the company's 1994 privatization. It said the shares sold were subject to pre-emptive rights from Elf's other core shareholders.</p>
<p>The buyer, or buyers, are not known as yet.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
